    "decision": "revised",
    "changes": "Automated run (3 stations, 30-100 s, Mw 6.4 at 1 km) replaced. Depth FIXED at 3 km (reviewer's call: shallow event). Band 10-50 s. Station set and time shifts from an iteration at 3 km: every subset of 15 candidates ranked with mttime's cross-correlation shifts, then each station's shift refined on a -8..+8 s grid (own VR >= 25, >= 4 azimuth sectors, DC >= 60). Final 6 stations HPRZ LTZ DBHZ ERWZ RPZ DSZ, shifts HPRZ +1 LTZ +1 DBHZ +2 ERWZ +2 RPZ +4 DSZ +2 s. SMRZ KHZ CVZ THZ OXZ excluded (bad records, OXZ 10x amplitude).",
    "notes": "At 3 km: Mw 4.86, VR 87, DC 68, 239/58/155 and 338/69/34, 5 sectors, every own VR above 79. Strike agrees with the SKHASH first-motion plane (243/88/180) and USGS Mwr 4.8; the dip is 58 against 88 because the depth is fixed shallow. Depth is not resolved by the waveform data alone: the same search free in depth gives VR 89-92 at 8-10 km with the vertical strike-slip mechanism 243/74/172 (4 stations HPRZ LTZ IFMZ DSZ, or 5 with INZ, DC 61). Mw 4.8-4.9 at every depth and station set. GeoNet 5 km is an operator-assigned placeholder; USGS 13 km."
